  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\n   We aim to reduce the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap bound by improving upon the current 0.381326 record. The key insight is to use multi-resolution optimization: first optimize at a lower resolution to find promising candidates, then refine those candidates at high resolution.\n\n   The strategy involves:\n   - Using two different base shapes (triangular and radially symmetric) for initial exploration\n   - Implementing a repair mechanism to handle boundary violations\n   - Employing a time-based stopping criterion to ensure optimization completes within the budget\n   - Using both the provided triangular parent and a radially symmetric candidate for diverse exploration\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n   The optimization variables are the values of h in the first half of the domain [0,1]. The full function is constructed by concatenation: h_full = np.concatenate([h_vec, h_vec[::-1]].\n\n   Objective function:\n      C5 = max_k $\\int$ h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx \n   \u2192 Converted to discrete correlation: $\\max$ $\\left| \\left( h \\otimes (1-h) \\right)_{n+1+k} \\right|$ for k=-(n-1) to (n-1)\n\n   Constraints:\n      0.0 \u2264 h_vec[i] \u2264 1.0 for all i\n      $\\sum$ h_vec[i] = n_points/2\n\n   Formulated in terms of the first half of the function.\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n   \u03b5 Define lower resolution (n_base) and higher resolution (n_full) = 280\n   \u03b5 Base resolution = 140 (to allow more samples)\n   \u03b5 For each shape:\n        candidate = function returning a base configuration\n        mirror to full length\n        optimize at base resolution with method=SLSQP:\n            bounds = (0,1)\n            constraints = sum == n_base/2\n            use repair mechanism when values exceed [0,1]\n   \u03b5 Convert best candidate to 280-point version via interpolation\n   \u03b5 Perform high-resolution optimization using the best candidate as initial guess\n\n   \u03b5 Repair function:\n        Clip values to [0,1]\n        Then scale to meet integral constraint\n\n   \u03b5 Objective function:\n        Correlate h_full and 1-h_full (mode='full')\n        Return max correlation value multiplied by dx=2/280\n\n4. Search choices and variations:\n   - Two base shapes: effective_triangular and efficient_radial\n   - Repair after every function evaluation\n   - 10 trials per shape (one per seed=42+idx)\n   - One shape guided optimization at higher base resolution\n\n   - Choose the best candidate between triangular and radial and use its high-resolution interpolation as final seed\n\n5. Budget and robustness:\n   - Time estimates (lower resolution < full resolution)\n   - Each optimization limited by time rather than evaluations\n   - Keep track of elapsed time for each dimension/stage\n   - Return the best candidate found, regardless of interpolation\n\n6. Validation and score calculation:\n   - Final validation done with 280-point function and full correlation\n   - Check that all values in h are between 0 and 1\n   - Check integral matches: sum(h)*dx_full \u2248 1",
